From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] i2c: tegra: always reset controller on transfer error

L4T 35.7.0 stopped calling tegra_i2c_init() from
tegra_i2c_error_recover() when multimaster_mode is set, so that an abrupt
reset does not disturb other masters on the bus. i2c@c240000 on Xavier AGX
is multi-master, so after 35.7.0 the controller is not reset after a
failed transfer there.

With i2c-tegra dynamic debug on a Xavier AGX, a transfer completes with a
NACK (msg_err=1) about 14 s after boot. Unpatched, no reset follows, and
the next transfer, about 50 s later (an ina3221 access), times out:

  tegra-i2c c240000.i2c: I2C transfer timed out
  ina3221 1-0040: Unable to reset device

With the reset restored, the controller is reset right after the NACK and
the later transfer completes. The timeout message itself comes from
tegra_i2c_xfer_msg(), which already resets unconditionally; the guard
acts on the earlier NACK.

Restore the 35.6.5 behaviour of always resetting the controller. This does
not explain why the first transfer NACKs, or why the controller that was
not reset then times out 50 s later. The tegra_i2c_change_clock_rate()
return value fix from the same upstream change is not reverted.
---
 drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-tegra.c | 6 +-----
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 5 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-tegra.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-tegra.c
@@ -1500,11 +1500,7 @@
 	if (i2c_dev->msg_err == I2C_ERR_NONE)
 		return 0;
 
-	/* Do not reset the controller if multimaster mode is enabled.
-	 * Abrupt reset may disturb the other masters on the bus.
-	 */
-	if (!i2c_dev->multimaster_mode)
-		tegra_i2c_init(i2c_dev);
+	tegra_i2c_init(i2c_dev);
 
 	/* start recovery upon arbitration loss in single master mode.
 	 * Return the appropriate error otherwise
